@format 1
@id media-preview.in-edit
@title In Edit
@section Media preview
@area In Edit
@entry edit-path-change, edit-media-change
@summary Show Edit-specific selected-path preview loading, mpv eligibility, and restoration when viewer media publication occurs.
@related media-selection.common.files-selection, media-preview.common.viewer-gate, media-preview.common.media-publication, media-preview.common.mpv-preview, media-loading.in-edit
@tag media
@tag preview
@tag edit

@alias edit = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PEditTab
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer

[edit-path-change] Edit Files current-path event <input>
~ This starts when the selected file changes in the Edit tab.
[Technical explanation]
= PListPathChange synchronously delivered the current path to PEditPathShow.
> edit-path-result

[edit-media-change] Edit viewer-media event <input>
~ This starts when the Edit preview finishes changing its media.
[Technical explanation]
= PViewerMediaRaise reached Edit's PViewerMediaChange subscriber during shared preview publication.
> edit-restore

[edit-path-result] Edit selected-path adapter <decision>
~ The Edit tab decides what to do with the newly selected media path.
[Technical explanation]
- Log the selected file/persistence state, ignore blank selection, and request a nonblank source from the Edit viewer @ edit.PEditPathShow(...)
  @ property viewer.PViewerEditEligible
! The Edit viewer is constructed with PViewerEditEligible=true; current non-Edit media-tab viewers leave it false, so only Edit can make Viewer gate select configured mpv.
? "Nonblank current path" > map:media-preview.common.viewer-gate
? "Blank current path" > edit-no-request

[edit-restore] Restore Edit state for current viewer source <process>
~ This step handles restore Edit state for current viewer source.
[Technical explanation]
- PEditCropRestore ignores the LCargo argument and restores source-specific/carried state from the viewer's current PViewerSourcePath and crop state when this subscriber runs @ edit.PEditCropRestore(...)
  @ property viewer.PViewerSourcePath
! Successful Flyleaf/mpv commits assign PViewerSourcePath before publication. Backend failure publishes without replacing it, so failure restoration targets the previously committed source. Viewer close clears it before publishing empty cargo.
> edit-restored

[edit-no-request] Edit preview request omitted <output>
~ This path ends with edit preview request omitted.
[Technical explanation]
= Edit logs the empty selection and does not call the shared viewer-preview pipeline.

[edit-restored] Edit preview state synchronized <output>
~ This path ends with edit preview state synchronized.
[Technical explanation]
= Edit crop/edit state reflects the viewer source and state current at publication time, which can differ from a failure cargo's requested path.
